{"abstract":[{"text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By the end of this guide you will have a game with two rooms, one object, one rule, and a test that plays it. It assumes you can write basic Swift; it assumes nothing about interactive fiction.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer to start from something that already runs? The repo ships a complete starter package at ","type":"text"},{"code":"Templates\/NewGame","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — copy it out, rename it, and skim this guide for the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" behind each piece.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Add Gnusto to your package","type":"heading","anchor":"Add-Gnusto-to-your-package","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add Gnusto as a dependency, list it in your executable target, and give the test target the ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoTestSupport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product (it links the toolchain’s Testing library, so it belongs in test targets only):","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ swift-tools-version: 6.2","import PackageDescription","","let package = Package(","    name: \"MyGame\",","    platforms: [.macOS(.v15)],","    dependencies: [","        .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/Gnusto\", from: \"0.1.0\")","    ],","    targets: [","        .executableTarget(","            name: \"MyGame\",","            dependencies: [","                .product(name: \"Gnusto\", package: \"Gnusto\")","            ]","        ),","        .testTarget(","            name: \"MyGameTests\",","            dependencies: [","                \"MyGame\",","                .product(name: \"GnustoTestSupport\", package: \"Gnusto\"),","            ]","        ),","    ]",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Gnusto needs a Swift 6.2 toolchain and the Swift 6 language mode. The ","type":"text"},{"code":".macOS(.v15)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" floor above is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Synchronization.Mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; Linux is tested in CI and needs no platform line. iOS is supported too, at ","type":"text"},{"code":".iOS(.v18)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the same reason. Add that line if your game is an app rather than a terminal program, and give it an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of its own — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Declare a game","type":"heading","anchor":"Declare-a-game","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A game is a single type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Start with just a title and an intro:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","","struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" requires an ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but Swift synthesizes it for free as long as every stored property has a default value — which they always will here, since rooms, items, and state are declared with initializers.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Add a room","type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-room","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" as a stored property. The property name (","type":"text"},{"code":"hall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") becomes the room’s internal identity; the ","type":"text"},{"code":"name(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" trait is what the player sees.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","","    let hall = Location {","        name(\"Entrance Hall\")","        description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","    }","","    var map: WorldMap {","        player.starts(in: hall)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block is where geography and starting positions live. ","type":"text"},{"code":"player.starts(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" places the player; without it, the game has nowhere to begin.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Run it","type":"heading","anchor":"Run-it","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two lines turn a game value into a running session:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" validates the game and builds its initial state up front — a mistake like an exit to an undeclared room is caught here, as a thrown ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", not at runtime. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" runs the prompt\/parse\/perform\/print loop, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reads from and writes to the terminal.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wrap it in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"do","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"catch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your ","type":"text"},{"code":"main.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","","do {","    let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","    await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()","} catch {","    print(\"Couldn't start the game: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Run ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and you can already ","type":"text"},{"code":"look","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" around and try to move.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Add a second room and connect them","type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-second-room-and-connect-them","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Exits are declared on locations in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. Each directional method (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", …) is an ordinary property reference, so a typo or a renamed room is a compile error, not a broken game.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let hall = Location {","    name(\"Entrance Hall\")","    description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","}","","let library = Location {","    name(\"Dusty Library\")","    description(\"Shelves sag under mildewed books. The hall lies south.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Exits are one-directional by design — declare both ","type":"text"},{"code":"hall.north(library)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"library.south(hall)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if you want the player to be able to walk back.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Add a thing","type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-thing","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" the same way, then place it in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    adjectives(\"brass\", \"old\")","    description(\"An old brass lantern, its glass sooty but intact.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","    lantern.starts(in: library)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Now the player can walk ","type":"text"},{"code":"north","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"examine lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"take lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and see it in their ","type":"text"},{"code":"inventory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" let them type ","type":"text"},{"code":"take brass lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"take old lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a phrase has to end on a noun, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"take brass","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on its own is not one of them. The last word of ","type":"text"},{"code":"name(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (“lantern”) is the noun the parser keys on.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything you declare is split into words the same way the parser splits what the player types — lowercased, a trailing possessive dropped, every other punctuation mark a separator. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"name(\"Mrs. Vane\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" prints its period and answers to ","type":"text"},{"code":"mrs vane","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"adjectives(\"master's\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the same declaration as ","type":"text"},{"code":"adjectives(\"master\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Write the second: a declaration should read the way the parser stores it.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"React with a rule","type":"heading","anchor":"React-with-a-rule","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So far every verb uses its built-in behavior. To add your own logic, write a rule in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. Rules are ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hooks attached to a location, an item, or the whole world.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var rules: Rules {","    lantern.after(.take) {","        say(\"It's heavier than it looks.\")","    }","","    library.before(.go) {","        guard command.direction != .south else { return }","        try refuse(\"There's no exit that way — only back south to the hall.\")","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The first rule runs ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the player successfully takes the lantern and adds a line of flavor with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The second runs ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" movement in the library and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"s any direction but south. Inside a rule body, bare identifiers like ","type":"text"},{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" refer to the live turn — reading and writing them touches the current game state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To learn what rules can do — the phases, the ordering, and the difference between ","type":"text"},{"code":"refuse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"reply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"say","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"end","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Test it","type":"heading","anchor":"Test-it","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A play session is just typed input and printed output, so the natural test plays a scripted session and asserts on the transcript:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","struct MyGameTests {","    @Test func theLanternIsWhereTheBreezeSaysItIs() async throws {","        let transcript = try await play(MyGame(), [\"north\", \"take lantern\"])","        expectInOrder(transcript, [\"Dusty Library\", \"Taken.\"])","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"play","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" boots the game and feeds it each command; ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectInOrder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" asserts the beats appear in order and shows the full transcript when one doesn’t. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for turn slicing and pinning the random stream.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"A fuller example","type":"heading","anchor":"A-fuller-example","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Gnusto ships with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cloak of Darkness","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", Roger Firth’s classic one-room demonstration game, as its ","type":"text"},{"code":"CloakOfDarkness","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target. It exercises nearly every feature in a page of code — dark rooms, a wearable cloak, scored actions, a losing state, and per-turn rules — and is worth reading start to finish once the basics click.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Next steps","type":"heading","anchor":"Next-steps","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Templates\/NewGame"},{"type":"text","text":" in the repo — the complete starter package this guide builds up to"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — how declarations, identity, and live references fit together"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — exactly what happens each turn"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — the full vocabulary of game logic"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — teach the parser new words with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#verb"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — transcript tests with GnustoTestSupport"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — carry your own data on entities and in globals"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"Getting Started with Gnusto","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted"]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/CustomFrontEnds":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/customfrontends","type":"topic","title":"Custom Front Ends","abstract":[{"text":"Putting the engine behind something that is not a terminal.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":